    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "7 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2026-07-29 22:06:00 MDT Expires: 2026-07-29 22:45:00 MDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building. Target Area: Great Salt Lake Desert and Mountains; Eastern Box Elder County At 1006 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 19 miles northwest of Great Salt Lake North of the Causeway, or 31 miles southwest of Snowville, moving northeast at 35 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible.\nLocations impacted include... Howell, Great Salt Lake North of the Causeway, Locomotive Springs, Gunnison Island, Promontory, and Golden Spike Historic Site.",
